  "term": "sciatic nerve",
  "definition": "The sciatic nerve is a large nerve that arises from the lower spinal cord in the lumbar and sacral regions and provides movement and sensation to the lower limb. It is the main continuation of the sacral plexus and divides into the tibial and peroneal nerves.",
